      "summaries": {
        "en": "Omarchy is an opinionated Linux distribution that prioritizes aesthetic design and modern user experience while maintaining practical functionality. It achieves this through carefully curated defaults, pre-configured tools, and a cohesive visual language that reduces setup complexity. Developers can use Omarchy as a ready-to-use development environment, customize its configurations for specific workflows, or study its design choices to inform their own system setups.",
        "zh": "Omarchy 是一款具有鲜明设计理念的 Linux 发行版，旨在提供美观、现代且开箱即用的桌面体验。它通过精心挑选的默认软件、预配置的开发工具和统一的视觉设计，减少了用户繁琐的系统配置工作。其核心在于将开发者的最佳实践固化为默认设置，让用户能立即投入高效工作。你可以直接将其作为日常开发环境，借鉴其配置方案优化自己的系统，或基于其框架构建定制化的 Linux 变体。",
        "es": "Omarchy is an opinionated Linux distribution that prioritizes aesthetic design and modern user experience while maintaining practical functionality. It achieves this through carefully curated defaults, pre-configured tools, and a cohesive visual language that reduces setup complexity. Developers can use Omarchy as a ready-to-use development environment, customize its configurations for specific workflows, or study its design choices to inform their own system setups.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "omarchy gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Omarchy is an opinionated Linux distribution that prioritizes aesthetic design and modern user experience while maintaining practical functionality. It achieves this through carefully curated defaults, pre-configured tools, and a cohesive visual language that reduces setup complexity. Developers can use Omarchy as a ready-to-use development environment, customize its configurations for specific workflows, or study its design choices to inform their own system setups.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/basecamp/omarchy for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
