      "summaries": {
        "en": "Claude Scientific Skills is an open-source toolkit that transforms Claude AI into a specialized research assistant, addressing the challenge of applying AI to complex scientific workflows without extensive coding. It works by providing modular 'skills'—pre-built functions for tasks like data analysis, bioinformatics, and literature review—that users can combine like building blocks. Researchers can integrate these skills into their projects via Python to automate analyses, explore datasets, or draft technical documents, making advanced AI assistance accessible for experimental and computational work.",
        "zh": "Claude Scientific Skills 是一个开源工具包，旨在将 Claude AI 转化为专业科研助手。它通过模块化的“技能”覆盖数据分析、生物信息学等任务，用户可灵活组合使用。该工具将科研流程拆解为可复用组件，降低了 AI 集成门槛，支持研究人员通过 Python 嵌入项目，实现实验分析自动化、基因组数据探索及论文辅助撰写，适用于生物信息学、药物发现等领域的快速原型验证与实验增强。",
        "es": "Claude Scientific Skills is an open-source toolkit that transforms Claude AI into a specialized research assistant, addressing the challenge of applying AI to complex scientific workflows without extensive coding. It works by providing modular 'skills'—pre-built functions for tasks like data analysis, bioinformatics, and literature review—that users can combine like building blocks. Researchers can integrate these skills into their projects via Python to automate analyses, explore datasets, or draft technical documents, making advanced AI assistance accessible for experimental and computational work.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "claude-scientific-skills stands out for agent-skills, ai-scientist, and bioinformatics in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Claude Scientific Skills is an open-source toolkit that transforms Claude AI into a specialized research assistant, addressing the challenge of applying AI to complex scientific workflows without extensive coding. It works by providing modular 'skills'—pre-built functions for tasks like data analysis, bioinformatics, and literature review—that users can combine like building blocks. Researchers can integrate these skills into their projects via Python to automate analyses, explore datasets, or draft technical documents, making advanced AI assistance accessible for experimental and computational work.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/K-Dense-AI/claude-scientific-skills for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
