      "summaries": {
        "en": "Firecrawl is a web scraping API that converts entire websites into clean, structured data formats like Markdown, solving the challenge of preparing web content for AI applications. It intelligently navigates sites, extracts meaningful content while filtering noise, and outputs LLM-ready data through a simple API. Developers can use it to build AI agents that process real-time web information, create custom datasets for training, or enhance search applications with structured web knowledge.",
        "zh": "Firecrawl是一个专为AI设计的网页数据提取工具，它能将整个网站转化为结构化的Markdown或JSON数据，解决了为大型语言模型准备网络内容的难题。其核心技术在于智能爬取和内容清洗，能够自动识别并提取网页中的核心信息，同时过滤广告、导航等干扰元素，输出干净、可直接用于AI处理的数据格式。开发者可通过其API快速构建能够实时处理网络信息的AI代理，创建定制化的训练数据集，或为搜索应用增强结构化知识库，让AI更有效地利用网络资源。",
        "es": "Firecrawl is a web scraping API that converts entire websites into clean, structured data formats like Markdown, solving the challenge of preparing web content for AI applications. It intelligently navigates sites, extracts meaningful content while filtering noise, and outputs LLM-ready data through a simple API. Developers can use it to build AI agents that process real-time web information, create custom datasets for training, or enhance search applications with structured web knowledge.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "firecrawl stands out for ai, ai-agents, and ai-crawler in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Firecrawl is a web scraping API that converts entire websites into clean, structured data formats like Markdown, solving the challenge of preparing web content for AI applications. It intelligently navigates sites, extracts meaningful content while filtering noise, and outputs LLM-ready data through a simple API. Developers can use it to build AI agents that process real-time web information, create custom datasets for training, or enhance search applications with structured web knowledge.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/firecrawl/firecrawl for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
